WEBVTT

NOTE target-profiles: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.351
Save your station targets under a name.

V0-2
00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:07.200
Then switch the whole course
to them in one action.

V1a-1
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.600
Click the gear in the toolbar.
The Settings dialog opens.

V1b-1
00:00:22.173 --> 00:00:24.703
Then click Target
Profiles in the left rail.

V2a-1
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.010
The tab lists five profile
slots for each Lynx course.

V2b-1
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.040
A profile stores one Target VWC
per station, and nothing else.

V2c-1
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.710
Name a profile for the
condition, such as Overseed.

V2d-1
00:00:44.823 --> 00:00:48.768
To capture your targets, mark the
slot under Update from Current.

V2d-2
00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.993
Nothing is captured until you save.

V3a-1
00:00:56.276 --> 00:01:00.036
To apply a profile, choose it
under Apply Profile, then confirm.

V3b-1
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.754
A profile matches stations by name.

V3b-2
00:01:03.854 --> 00:01:07.470
A renamed or renumbered station
won't match an old profile.

V3c-1
00:01:08.576 --> 00:01:11.046
Stations added after
capture keep their target.

V4a-1
00:01:12.926 --> 00:01:16.806
Read Target VWC on a few stations.
They match the profile.

V4b-1
00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:22.173
A profile applies course-wide, so check
the Suggested column before you push.
